{
  "about": "Decision 076 S5, PLAYS-DESIGN 2.10: where a reader's mark lands. Every stack runs these cases: `snap` grows a selection [start, end) in `text` to whole words (null when only space is selected); `point` is where a breath, pause or beat goes for a selection ending at `end`; `anchor` makes `mark` (line, start, end, kind) on `before` with that stack's make(), then re-anchors it to `after` with place(): `want` is the line id and offsets it lands at, or \"lost\" when it is kept, untouched, as not placed. Offsets count into the line's printed words (lineText: a speech's pieces joined by one space, else its source).",
  "snap": [
    {"text": "Why not? Never mind why.", "start": 11, "end": 14, "want": [9, 14]},
    {"text": "Why not? Never mind why.", "start": 8, "end": 9, "want": null},
    {"text": "Why not? Never mind why.", "start": 9, "end": 21, "want": [9, 23]},
    {"text": "It is the first in which _I_ have been serious.", "start": 26, "end": 27, "want": [25, 28]},
    {"text": "a well-known  face", "start": 4, "end": 6, "want": [2, 12]},
    {"text": "  Away!  ", "start": 0, "end": 9, "want": [2, 7]}
  ],
  "point": [
    {"text": "Yes--the first thing tomorrow morning, and then", "end": 33, "want": 38},
    {"text": "Yes--the first thing tomorrow morning, and then", "end": 38, "want": 38},
    {"text": "Yes--the first thing tomorrow morning, and then", "end": 39, "want": 38},
    {"text": "What, ho! Away.", "end": 2, "want": 5},
    {"text": "Done", "end": 4, "want": 4}
  ],
  "anchor": [
    {
      "name": "same revision: placed as stored",
